    "ruleType": "army-rule",
    "summary": "As [your Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase) begins, your **ADEPTUS CUSTODES** units that have this ability become **readied**. While a unit of yours is **readied**, you can pick a ka'tah ability from the list below for it to use, and it then stops being **readied**. Every ka'tah ability states its own timing and what it does to the unit that uses it.\n\n**Designer's Note**: a token beside each **readied** unit helps; take it away once that unit stops being **readied**.\n\nThe ka'tah abilities are:\n\n- **Conversai**: in [your Command phase](vsdata:core-rule/command-phase), pick a **readied** unit of yours. It can still start an [action](vsdata:core-rule/actions) while in [Engagement Range](vsdata:core-rule/engagement-range) of an enemy unit or while **battle-shocked**, and can still shoot after it starts one, for the rest of the turn.\n- **Calistus**: in [your Movement phase](vsdata:core-rule/movement-phase), as a **readied** unit of yours is **selected to move**, it can pass through models of any type while it makes a [normal move](vsdata:core-rule/normal-move), [advance move](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move) or [fall-back move](vsdata:core-rule/fall-back).\n- **Salvus**: in [your Shooting phase](vsdata:core-rule/shooting-phase), as a **readied** unit of yours is **selected to shoot**, it can disregard any modifier to its BS, its [Hit rolls](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls) and its [Wound rolls](vsdata:core-rule/wound-rolls).\n- **Dacatarai**: as [either player's Fight phase](vsdata:core-rule/fight-phase) begins, pick a **readied** unit of yours. Its melee attacks against an enemy unit that is not a **MONSTER** or **VEHICLE** unit can re-roll 1s to [Hit](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls).\n- **Kaptaris**: as [either player's Fight phase](vsdata:core-rule/fight-phase) begins, pick a **readied** unit of yours. Melee attacks against it get -1 to [Hit](vsdata:core-rule/hit-rolls).\n- **Rendax**: in [either player's Fight phase](vsdata:core-rule/fight-phase), as a **readied** unit of yours is **selected to fight**, pick one of your **readied** units. Its melee attacks get **[[LETHAL HITS: MONSTER/VEHICLE]](vsdata:weapon-ability/lethal-hits)**.\n\n**Favoured Ka'tah**: every Detachment tagged 'Unique: Shield Host' names one ka'tah ability as its Favoured Ka'tah, and with that Detachment, that ka'tah ability also gives the extra effect the Detachment lists. For example, with the Solar Watch Detachment, a **readied** unit you pick Calistus for gets +2\" M as well as the usual effect of Calistus.",
